          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Unlike a reaction that goes to completion—where one or more of the reactants is completely consumed and has a final concentration of 0—in a reversible reaction at equilibrium, none of the products or the reactants will have a concentration of 0. In this unit, we use tables like this one to help guide us through equilibrium calculations."
              }
            ],
            "id": "1zd82abx6icg1a0",
            "type": "p"
          }
